tler</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><source>Marketing for nonprofit organizations</source><year>1975</year><publisher-name>Englewood Cliffs, NJ: Prentice Hall</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bowen</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Moinpour</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Andersen</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Meischke</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Cochrane</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Miller S, Bowen DJ, Croyle R, Rowland J</surname></name></person-group><source>Creation of a framework for public health intervention design</source><publisher-name>Handbook of Behavior and Cancer American Psychological Association Press</publisher-name><comment></comment></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diehr</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Derleth</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Newman</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Cai</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How many sick persons will   there be?</article-title><source>Research on Aging</source><year>2007</year></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Vital and Health Statistics</collab></person-group><source>Americans assess their health: United States, 1987. Series 10. Data from the National Health Interview Survey. No. 174</source><year>1990</year><publisher-name>Hyattsville, MD: U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Public Health Service, Center for Disease Control, National Center for Health Statistics</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>MEPSnet</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.meps.ahrq.gov/MEPSnet/HC/MEPSnetHC.asp"/></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patrick</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Starks</surname><given-names>HE</given-names></name><name><surname>Cain</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Uhlman</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Pearlman</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measuring Preferences for Health States Worse than Death</article-title><source>Medical Decision Making</source><year>1994</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8152361</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/0272989X9401400102</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Stata ado file created by Margaret Weden</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ssc.wisc.edu/~mweden/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crimmins</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayward</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Saito</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changing mortality and morbidity rates and the health status and life expectancy of the older population</article-title><source>Demography</source><year>1994</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>175</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8005340</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/2061913</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boult</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Altmann</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilbertson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kane</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decreasing disability in the 21<sup>st </sup>century: the future effects of controlling six fatal and nonfatal conditions</article-title><source>American Journal of Public Health</source><year>1996</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>1388</fpage><lpage>1923</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8876506</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cornoni-Huntley</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Foley</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Guralnik</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Co-morbidity analysis: a strategy for understanding mortality, disability and the use of health care facilities of older persons</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiol</source><year>1991</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>S8</fpage><lpage>S17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9119546</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mathers</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gains in health expectancy from the elimination of diseases among older persons</article-title><source>Disabil Rehabil</source><year>1999</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>211</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10381233</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/096382899297639</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pamuk</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagener</surname><given-names>DK</gi